.TH STOMARCHY 1 "2026-07-26" "stomarchy 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stomarchy \- safely preserve append-only Omarchy Quattro customizations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stomarchy
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stomarchy
stores customization files below
.IR ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/stomarchy
while always managing live Omarchy targets below
.IR ~/.config .
Append-only adapters restore the current Omarchy original and add one marked
import block. Full-file adapters copy user-owned files without injecting an
Omarchy baseline or import.
.PP
On first
.BR add ,
the edited target must contain the matching Omarchy original as an exact byte
prefix. The remaining EOF suffix is stored verbatim. In-place edits, deletions,
reordering, and partial rewrites are refused without changing either file.
Afterward, edit the tracked tweak and use
.B link
instead of editing the assembled target.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "add [-n|--dry-run] " FILE
Capture an exact EOF suffix, or store a supported full file. The deprecated
.B --preview
option is an alias for
.BR --dry-run .
.TP
.BI "link [-n|--dry-run] [--force] [" FILE ]
Assemble one target or every tracked target. Direct target drift is refused by
default.
.B --force
overrides a conflict after writing a timestamped recovery snapshot.
.TP
.BI "remove [-n|--dry-run] [--force] [" FILE ]
Restore append-only targets successfully before deleting their tracked tweaks.
Full-file targets, including
.IR ~/.inputrc ,
are left intact. With no
.IR FILE ,
process every tracked tweak.
.TP
.B sync [-n|--dry-run] [--all] [--force]
Refresh tracked targets from current Omarchy originals and retain imports.
The default is tracked-only.
.B --all
covers the complete Quattro config mirror and requires
.BR --force .
.TP
.B wipe [-n|--dry-run] [--all] [--force]
Restore tracked append-only targets without imports while retaining tweak
files. User-owned full-file targets are left intact. The default is
tracked-only;
.B --all
requires
.BR --force .
.TP
.B status [--check] [--porcelain]
List tracked files in deterministic order.
.B --check
returns a failure status for actionable problems.
.B --porcelain
prints a target, a tab, and comma-separated tags.
.TP
.BI "help [" COMMAND ]
Show general or command-specific help.
.SH ADAPTERS
.SS Append-only overlays
.TP
.B hypr/*.lua
Loaded with
.BR dofile() .
The captured suffix must pass
.B luac -p
as a standalone EOF chunk. Quattro exposes the global
.B hl
and
.B o
APIs to these chunks.
.TP
.B ghostty/config
Loaded with
.BR config-file .
.TP
.B kitty/*.conf
Loaded with
.BR include .
.TP
.B tmux/*.conf
Loaded with
.BR source-file .
.TP
.B foot/*.ini
Loaded with
.BR include .
Stomarchy reopens
.B [main]
before the directive and checks the assembled target with
.BR "foot -C" .
.TP
.B ~/.bashrc
Loaded with Bash
.BR source .
Its Omarchy original is
.IR $OMARCHY_ROOT/default/bashrc ,
where
.I OMARCHY_ROOT
means the source root selected by the resolution order below.
.SS Full-file tracking
.TP
.B ~/.inputrc
Stored and restored as a complete user-owned file. No
.B $include
or Omarchy baseline is injected.
.TP
.B ~/.config/uwsm/default
Stored and restored as Quattro's optional complete user-owned file.
.PP
Hyprland
.BR *.conf ,
.IR uwsm/env ,
arbitrary
.BR *.sh ,
and every unregistered format are refused.
.SH CONFLICTS AND RECOVERY
Hashes below
.IR ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/stomarchy
record the Omarchy original, assembled target, and tweak. They distinguish an
upstream Omarchy change from a direct edit to a managed target.
.PP
Forced writes save affected targets and tweaks below a timestamped
.I recovery
directory in the state directory before replacement. Ordinary tracked
operations rely on conflict detection and atomic replacement and do not make
unconditional backups.
.SH STATUS TAGS
.TP
.B linked
The target exactly matches its expected assembled or full-file content.
.TP
.B no-op
An append-only tweak is empty.
.TP
.B tweak-changed
The tracked tweak changed while the managed target remained untouched; run
.BR link .
.TP
.B upstream-changed
The Omarchy original changed while the managed target remained untouched; run
.BR sync .
.TP
.B unlinked
The target is an unassembled baseline or a full file has not been copied.
.TP
.B drift
The live target was edited directly and will not be overwritten without
.BR --force .
.TP
.BR missing-target ", " missing-original ", " unsupported ", " invalid-tweak
.TQ
.BR malformed-markers ", " invalid-baseline ", " unsafe-target ", " unsafe-tweak
Actionable safety or compatibility failures.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STOMARCHY_OMARCHY_ROOT
Highest-priority Omarchy source root override.
.TP
.B OMARCHY_PATH
Production Omarchy source root when no Stomarchy-specific override is set.
.TP
.B STOMARCHY_OMARCHY_CONFIG_DIR
Compatibility override for only the Omarchy
.I config
mirror. When no root variable is set, its parent is treated as the Omarchy
root.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Controls Stomarchy repository storage only. Live targets remain below
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Controls baseline hashes, the mutation lock, and recovery snapshots.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colored diagnostics when present. Color is also disabled off a TTY.
.SH OMARCHY RESOLUTION
The source root is selected in this order:
.BR STOMARCHY_OMARCHY_ROOT ,
.BR OMARCHY_PATH ,
.IR /usr/share/omarchy ,
then
.IR ~/.local/share/omarchy .
Trailing slashes and lexical path components are normalized.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded and
.B status --check
found no actionable problems.
.TP
.B 1
An operational, validation, conflict, or status-check failure occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage was invalid.
.TP
.B 130, 143
The process was interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
STOMARCHY_OMARCHY_ROOT=~/Projects/omarchy stomarchy status
stomarchy add -n ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
stomarchy add ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
$EDITOR ~/.config/stomarchy/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
stomarchy link
stomarchy sync --dry-run
stomarchy wipe
stomarchy sync --all --force
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/stomarchy
Version-controllable tracked tweaks.
.TP
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/stomarchy
Machine-local hashes, mutation lock, and recovery snapshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR flock (1),
.BR foot (1),
.BR lua (1)
